===== G3: the trial's own token claim vs the token's real locations =====
  7:# any real vault, `op`, or a real secret. HOME/TMPDIR are scratch; the dev root token is random,
  the token is passed on the command line:
    76:bao server -dev -dev-root-token-id="$TOK" -dev-listen-address="127.0.0.1:$PORT" >"$S/server.log" 2>&1 &
  and is therefore in the process argv, readable by any local user via /proc/<pid>/cmdline:
    mount: proc /proc proc rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,relatime 0 0
    /proc/self/cmdline mode: -r--r--r--
  the lane's own controls runner captured exactly that argv into a committed receipt:
    18:      p=${e#/proc/}; p=${p%/environ}; echo "reaped $p $(tr '\0' ' ' < /proc/$p/cmdline 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-80)"; kill "$p" 2>/dev/null
